Program Bug_2_59_SetSpriteLoc_No_Range_Check;
// Bug 2.59: SetSpriteLoc's own error message for its third argument
// ("bank") reads "must be constant 0-3", implying the value is range
// checked. It isn't: Methods6502::SetSpriteLoc (methods6502.cpp
// ~5847-5871) only verifies the argument is a compile-time constant at
// all (`qSharedPointerDynamicCast<NodeNumber>` non-null), never that
// num3->m_val is actually inside 0-3. A bank of 4 or higher compiles
// clean with no error.
//
// Inverted expectation (same shape as 2.25 in batch 5): the bug is a
// *missing* error, so clean compilation IS the currently-buggy state.
// Pre-fix: COMPILE_OK. Post-fix (once the documented 0-3 range check is
// actually implemented): this should become COMPILE_ERROR ("SetSpriteLoc
// parameter 2 (bank) must be constant 0-3"). No VICE step either way -
// what's being verified is the presence/absence of the compile-time
// check itself, not a runtime register value.
begin
	SetSpriteLoc(0, $80, 4); // bank=4, outside the documented 0-3 range
	sprite_color[0] := light_red;
	togglebit(sprite_bitmask, 0, 1);
	SpritePos(100,100,0);
	loop();
end.
